<div class="wrap">
<h1>entire-graph on Opus: what the tokens actually did</h1>
<p class="lede">Two independently sampled cells of SWE-bench Multilingual, Opus, with Anthropic's
published prompt given verbatim to both arms. The target was &minus;25%. Neither cell reached it, and
the reason is measurable rather than mysterious.</p>
<p class="meta">2026-08-03 &middot; 361 sessions &middot; 0.64B tokens &middot; $560 &middot; paired, geomean of per-instance ratios, bootstrap CI</p>

<div class="verdict">
  <div class="v"><div class="k">20-instance official</div><div class="n good">-11.2%</div>
    <div class="s">CI [-27.8, +9.6] &middot; n=20</div></div>
  <div class="v"><div class="k">rep30</div><div class="n good">-14.5%</div>
    <div class="s">CI [-29.7, +3.4] &middot; n=29</div></div>
  <div class="v"><div class="k">target</div><div class="n key">&minus;25%</div>
    <div class="s">not reached in either</div></div>
  <div class="v"><div class="k">winners</div><div class="n">12/20 &middot; 17/29</div>
    <div class="s">instances cheaper with the tool</div></div>
</div>
<p>Both cells agree within ~3 points, which retires the idea that the instance set was the problem:
rep30 read &minus;40.9% at n=4 and settled at -14.5% by n=29. Aggregate and geomean also agree
(-11.4% / -11.9%), so no single instance carries either result.</p>

<h2>Two laws that predict the outcome</h2>
<div class="law"><div class="eq">eg_ops = 14.16 + 0.588 &times; base_ops &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; break-even at 34.4</div>
<p>The tool's own op count is statistically flat between winners and losers (d =&nbsp;&minus;0.08, p&nbsp;=&nbsp;0.97).
The <em>baseline's</em> is decisive (d&nbsp;=&nbsp;+1.55, p&nbsp;=&nbsp;0.0069, AUC 0.865). The tool wins by replacing a
wasteful control, not by being clever. Rule accuracy 15/20.</p></div>
<div class="law"><div class="eq">log(token ratio) = 1.207 &times; log(op ratio) &nbsp;&nbsp; R&sup2; = 0.916</div>
<p>Cost is superlinear in message count because 95.7% of all tokens are <span class="inst">cache_read</span> &mdash;
every extra message re-reads the whole accumulated context. Confirmed out of sample: rep30 ops &minus;31.2%
predicted &minus;38.6%, measured &minus;40.9%.</p></div>

