<h2>The confirmed, untried lever: aim</h2>
<p>Measured on nine instances with gold lines resolved by locating hunk context in the base file
(hunk headers are invalid at the base commit &mdash; fmtlib is off by +272):</p>
<div class="verdict" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)">
  <div class="v"><div class="k">gold file in payload</div><div class="n good">9/9 &middot; 100%</div>
    <div class="s">recall is not the problem</div></div>
  <div class="v"><div class="k">gold line covered</div><div class="n bad">0/9 &middot; ~0%</div>
    <div class="s">the region is</div></div>
</div>
<p>Right file always, right region never. lucene is the clean case: the payload prints four spans from
the correct file &mdash; 34&ndash;36, 27, 181&ndash;188, 118&ndash;124 &mdash; and the gold line at 148 falls between them.
redis-10095 returns <span class="inst">t_list.c:577</span> (<span class="inst">lpopCommand</span>, a lexical
match on "LPOP") while the fix is at line 501, in the helper it <em>calls</em>.</p>
<p>Root cause, verified in source: <span class="inst">search_related.go:41</span> deliberately excludes
outgoing CALLS on the reasoning that callees are "already reached as co-members of the same unit", and
<span class="inst">searchRelatedUnitMemberLimit&nbsp;=&nbsp;12</span> disables that fallback above 12 members.
On a large unit neither route reaches the callee.</p>
<p>This is the only mechanism that explains the one result that held in all five Opus configurations:
<strong>pre-edit locate rose every time</strong>, +3.7% to +9%. The agent is handed the correct file at a
wrong offset, greps it anyway, and pays twice.</p>

<h2>Refuted, with the control that killed each</h2>
<p>A five-agent sweep produced 38 candidate defects; 27 of 28 adjudicated died on a winner control &mdash;
the same pattern is equally present in the instances the tool wins on.</p>
<div class="kill">
<div><b>no line numbers in bodies</b><span>true in 20/20 instances incl. every winner; numbering them also breaks Edit anchors</span></div>
<div><b>ungated impact chaining</b><span>off-gold-file target in 7/12 winners, worse in the two largest wins</span></div>
<div><b>boilerplate queries</b><span>2/6 control winners have them and still win</span></div>
<div><b>hits out of score order</b><span>5/20 payloads, including two winners</span></div>
<div><b>missing COVERING TEST</b><span>inverted &mdash; 50% of losers vs 8% of winners</span></div>
<div><b>lint-only VERIFY</b><span>lint-only is the <em>best</em> class at &minus;24.6%</span></div>
<div><b>re-hunting payload text</b><span>base rate: baseline greps the same strings at 2.42/session vs eg's 2.42</span></div>
<div><b>provisioning episodes</b><span>package-install <em>decreases</em> in losers, 0.62&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;0.38</span></div>
<div><b>use the graph more</b><span>tripling usage measured worse; caddy &minus;56%&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;&minus;13%</span></div>
<div><b>index the tests</b><span>4,748 test symbols added, search output byte-identical</span></div>
<div><b>wider windows</b><span>+18.9pt worse</span></div>
<div><b>payload token tax</b><span>5.16% of winners vs 5.19% of losers &mdash; identical</span></div>
</div>

